WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.382
Here is how CoCN works.

00:00:03.462 --> 00:00:06.843
First,

00:00:06.923 --> 00:00:10.305
permutation generation regresses an absolute
position for each node with an MLP on Laplacian-smoothed features,

00:00:10.385 --> 00:00:13.766
so similar nodes land nearby.

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:17.228
These form a relaxed permutation matrix,

00:00:17.308 --> 00:00:20.689
controlled by a factor tau that provably converges
to a true permutation.

00:00:20.769 --> 00:00:24.151
With nodes in a row,

00:00:24.231 --> 00:00:27.612
CoCN slides a kernel along the diagonal of the
permuted edge and node matrices,

00:00:27.692 --> 00:00:31.074
extracting node features and their structure together.

00:00:31.154 --> 00:00:34.535
Compressed pooling builds a hierarchy,

00:00:34.615 --> 00:00:37.997
and transposed convolution up-samples for predictions.

00:00:38.077 --> 00:00:41.458
Crucially, this cuts permutation modeling from n
factorial to n squared,

00:00:41.538 --> 00:00:44.920
letting it scale to large graphs.
